{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "bc5a28f5-113d-8b6e-92e7-08d1bd40b8ea",
  "created_at": "2026-03-10T09:38:07-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Teresa Vieira",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:34:40-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:34:44-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi. Teresa Vieira. I got a question about recycling. What's allowed in the bin now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:34:53-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. What are you trying to put in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:34:58-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Pizza boxes, for one. Glass jars and bottles. And those plastic clamshells, the ones the berries come in. I've heard different things."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:35:10-04:00",
      "duration": 28,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Glass bottles and jars are fine, just empty them and give them a quick rinse. Clamshells, the hard plastic ones, usually go in if they're clean. Pizza boxes are the tricky one. If it's greasy or has cheese stuck on it, that part goes in the trash. A clean top can go in recycling."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:35:38-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So tear it up. Clean part in, greasy part out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:35:44-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:35:46-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Is there a fee for any of that? For the recycling bin or whatever?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:35:54-04:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Regular curbside recycling pickup doesn't have a separate charge for what goes in the bin. If you're asking about a new or replacement bin, I'd have to look that up for you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:36:11-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, no, I got the bin. Just wanted to know nobody's gonna bill me for the glass."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:36:20-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:36:23-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. That's the way it goes, you hear a rumor and you wonder."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:36:30-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Is this for a place here in Newport? I can note the pickup area."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:36:38-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "238 Dixon Street. North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:36:41-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 238 Dixon. Do you want me to check your pickup day while I'm in here?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:36:50-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, go ahead. I think it's Thursday, but the holiday weeks mess me up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:36:58-04:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me see. [pause] Yes, Thursday for that block. Recycling alternates weeks, so check the calendar for which week is yours."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:37:09-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I got the calendar on the fridge. Fine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:37:14-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:37:17-04:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, the reason I'm even looking at this, my kid's been bringing home all kinds of lunch stuff since the school cafeteria changed the menu. Now there's all these containers. Kid's not pleased with the new food, either."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:37:37-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, that'll do it. Lots of packaging. Same rule on those, if it's clean and hard plastic, it can go in. Thin film and bags stay out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:37:51-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Film stays out. Got it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:37:55-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're all set then."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:37:58-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thanks. That's all I needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:38:01-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Teresa. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T09:38:05-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too."
    }
  ],
